# Review: CommercePlugin

49 items: 13 done, 9 untested, 8 partial, 11 diverged, 8 missing. The template pipeline is solid and unit-tested:
the mapping schemas, `bindRequest`, `extractResults`, the JSON Schema union and `applyProviderTemplate` all have
tests, and a `manual` agent test drives the provider skill through AnalyzeProvider and SetProviderTemplate against a
real page. Apart from that manual test, no test invokes an operation handler, and no story has a play function.

The code moved away from the spec in its data model and UI. `Search` keeps criteria in `params`, appends Results to a
backing feed (deduplicated by URL, accumulating across runs) instead of `results: Ref<Result>[]`, has no `status`, and
adds a star tag index. `Provider` has no `enabled` field, so nothing skips disabled providers. The criteria form and
the Run button live in the `SearchProperties` companion, not in SearchArticle; the result detail replaces the grid in
the same panel; ProviderArticle is a read-only preview with a Regenerate action that runs the skill agent through a
new `GenerateProviderTemplate` operation. RangeField exists but is not used.

Gaps that matter:

- **F-1.6 / RunSearch:** there is no `Provider.enabled`, so disabled providers cannot be skipped; RunSearch runs
  every provider in sequence and never clears or sets status.
- **Search model diverged:** F-3.2, F-3.4, F-3.5 and the `Search` type describe `status` and `results` refs that
  the code replaced with ephemeral UI state and a feed; the spec needs updating to the feed design.
- **No handler or UI tests:** RunSearch, RunProviderSearch and the Run button (T-3, T-4, T-5, T-7) are not
  exercised.

